1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,100
Mara: This week on Harbor Voices we ride
the first ferry of the morning.

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:10,900
{\an8}Mara: The timetable changed in October, so the
first crossing now leaves at 6:40 instead of 7:15.

3
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:17,300
Ines: I have captained the <i>Petrel</i> for eleven
years, and the early boat is mostly bakers and nurses.

4
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:24,000
Ines: We carry about ninety people and six
bicycles on a normal Tuesday.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,200
Mara: What happens when the fog comes in?

6
00:00:30,200 --> 00:00:39,500
Ines: We slow to four knots and sound the horn every two
minutes. The crossing takes twenty-five minutes instead of twelve.

7
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Ines: Nobody complains. They would rather be
late than swim.
